hadiths[121]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7679","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Umayy told us, Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Amer bin Saleh bin Rustum told us. Al-Khazzaz, Ayoub bin Musa bin Amr bin Saeed bin Al-Aas told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: “No father treats his child better than good manners.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7679 - Rather, it is a weak transmitter"
"7680","Abu Al-Hussein Ali bin Abdul-Rahman bin Issa Al-Subaie informed us, in Kufa, Ahmed bin Hazim Al-Ghafari told us, Malik bin Ismail, Nasih Abu Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Samak ibn Harb, on the authority of Jabir ibn Samurah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: “By God, for one of you to discipline his son is better for him than for him to give in charity every day half a saa’.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7680 - Abu Abdullah’s adviser perished"
"7681","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakkar bin Qutaybah Al-Qadi, in Egypt, told us, Safwan bin Issa told us, Al-Harith bin Abd told us. Al-Rahman bin Abi Dhabab, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “When He created God Almighty exalted Adam and breathed the spirit into him. He sneezed and said: Praise be to God. So he thanked God, God willing, and his Lord said to him: May God have mercy on you, O Adam. A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7681 - True"
"7682","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib Al-Dhabi, and Hisham bin Ali Al-Sadusi told us, saying: Musa bin Ismail Abu Salamah told us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: “When the spirit was blown into Adam and it reached the nostrils, he sneezed and said: Praise be to God.” Lord of the worlds. Then God, Blessed and Most High, said: May God have mercy on you. “absolutely true”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7682 - Sahih according to Muslim’s conditions"
"7683","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Hanthali told us about the Burdan Bridge, Abu Qalaba Al-Raqqashi told us, Abu Asim told us, Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Indeed, God Almighty loves sneezing.” Yawning is disliked, so if one of you sneezes and says: Praise be to God, everyone who hears him gloating is entitled to say: May God have mercy on you, and yawning is Satan, so if one of you yawns, let him repel it as much as he can, for if one of you yawns, he says: Here, Satan laughs at him. “This is a hadith. The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7683 - True"
"7684","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Abdullah bin Ayyash told me, about Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “When one of you sneezes, let him place his palms on His face and let him lower his voice. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7684 - True"
"7685","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar told us, about Hakim bin Aflah, on the authority of Abu Masoud, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “A Muslim has four duties towards another Muslim: he should answer him.” When he invites him, and visits him when he is sick, and smells him when he sneezes, and takes him to his funeral when he dies. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7685 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7686","Ali bin Ahmad bin Qarqoub Al-Tamar told us about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, On the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Indeed, God Almighty loves sneezing.” So when one of you sneezes, it is obligatory for everyone who heard him to say: May God have mercy on you. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and this A translation from which Abu Abdullah Al-Bukhari did not make any hadith permissible.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7686 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7687","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Qabbani told us, Amr bin Ali told us, Abu Aamir Al-Aqdi told us, Ibn Abi told us Dhi’ib, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Sneezing is from God And yawning is from Satan, so when one of you sneezes, it is obligatory for whoever hears him to say: May God have mercy on you.”"
"7688","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad told us, Musaddad told us, Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade people from sitting At the end of the ascents, they said: We cannot and do not tolerate that, O Messenger of God. He said: “But no, so they fulfilled her right.” They said: What is her right, O Messenger of God? He said: “Return the greeting, and praise the one who sneezes when he praises God, and lower the gaze and show the way.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7688 - True"
"7689","Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz informed us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: Two men sat with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, one of them more noble than the other. The sherif sneezed and did not thank God, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not smell him. Then the other sneezed and thanked God, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, smelled him and said: Al-Sharif: I sneezed, but you did not smell me, and this man sneezed, and I smelled him. He said: “You forgot God, so I forgot you, and this man mentioned God, so I remembered him.” True. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7689 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7690","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, Al-Qasim told us Ibn Malik Al-Muzani, Asim Ibn Kulayb told us, on the authority of Abu Burdah Ibn Abi Musa, who said: I witnessed Abu Musa while he was in the house of Umm Al-Fadl, and she sneezed. So I smelled it and sneezed, but he did not smell me. When I came to my mother, I told her. When Abu Musa came to her, she said to him: My son sneezed near you, but you did not smell him. And a woman sneezed and I smelled her, and he said: Your son sneezed and did not thank God, so I did not smell him. And she sneezed and thanked God so I smelled her. I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you sneezes and praises God, smell him, and if he does not thank God, do not smell him.” She said: Well done. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7690 - True"
"7691","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Musa bin Harun told us, Abu Al-Rabi’ Al-Harithi told us, and Muhammad bin Yahya told us Al-Qutay’i, they said: Ziyad bin Al-Rabi’ narrated to us, Al-Hadrami bin Lahiq narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, that a man sneezed in the presence of Abdullah bin Omar, may God be pleased with him. About them, he said: Praise be to God and peace be upon the Messenger of God. Ibn Omar said: I say praise be to God and peace be upon the Messenger of God, but not like this. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught us when one of us sneezes to say: “Praise be to God in every situation.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. It is strange in A translation of the sheikhs of Nafi’, but they did not narrate it: “It was narrated on the authority of the Commander of the Faithful, Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, on the subject, two hadiths that were unique According to their narration by Muhammad bin Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of his fathers, as for the first hadith from them.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7691 - Sahih Gharib"
"7692","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq Al-Basri told us, in Egypt, Saeed bin Amir told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of his brother Issa, on the authority of his father Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Abu Ayyub Al Ansari, May God be pleased with him. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The one who sneezes says: Praise be to God in every situation, and the one who smells him says: May God have mercy on you.” And he will respond to him, “May God guide you and set your mind right.” “This is one of the illusions of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, the Ansar jurist and judge.” May God Almighty have mercy on him. Were it not for what appeared of these illusions, the imams of hadith would not have attributed it to poor memorization and explanation of what I mentioned.”"
"7693","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, Ibn Abi Laila told us, my brother told me, On the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If one of you sneezes, let him say: Praise be to God in every condition.” And they should say to him: May God have mercy on you, and let him say: May God guide you and be reconcilable to you. As for the wording that the jurists of Kufa chose for the one who sneezes in The answer is in this greeting.”"
"7694","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Kamil bin Khalaf Al-Qadi told us, Abu Qalaba Abdul-Malik bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Raqqashi told me. My father, Ja’far bin Sulayman told us, Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib told us, Abu Abbas Ahmad bin Harun Al-Faqih told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us. Al-Makki, and Muhammad bin Ayyub Al-Razi, they said: Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Yunus told us, Abyad bin Aban Al-Qurashi told us, on the authority of Ata bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Sulami, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If If one of you sneezes, let him say: Praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds, and let him say: May God have mercy on you, and let him say: May God forgive us and you. This is a hadith that was not narrated from the chain of transmission. On the authority of Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, other than Ata bin Al-Sa’ib, Ja’far bin Suleiman Al-Dabai and Abyad were unique in narrating it from him. Ibn Aban Al-Qurashi, and the correct one about it is the narration of the imam, the memorizer, the master, Sufyan bin Saeed Al-Thawri, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib.”"
"7695","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Humaid bin Abbas Al-Ramli told us, Ma’mal bin Ismail told us, Sufyan told us, and Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Sufyan told us, Abu Al-Abbas Al-Mahboubi told us, Ahmad bin Sayyar, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Sufyan told us, Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Abu Hudhayfah, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Sulami, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: “If one of you sneezes, let him say: Praise be to God, and let him say: May God have mercy on you. Then when he is told: May God have mercy on you, let him say: May God forgive us and you. This is what is preserved from the words of Abdul By God, if the one who relies on his narration does not support it.”"
"7696","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Usayd bin Asim Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, On the authority of Sufyan, and Ibrahim bin Hatim Al-Hiri informed us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Sana’ani told us, in Sana’a, Muhammad bin Jasham Al-Sana’ani told us, Sufyan narrated to us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq narrated to us, and the wording is his. Abu Al-Muthanna narrated, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Mansour told me, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of another man, who said: We were with Salem bin Ubaid on a trip, and a man sneezed and said: Peace be upon you. He said: Peace be upon you and your mother. Then he asked him and he said: Perhaps you heard about that. He said: I do not like for you to mention my mother. Salem said: We were with the Prophet. Then a man sneezed and said: Peace be upon you. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Peace be upon you and your mother.” Then he said: “If one of you sneezes, let him say: Praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds, or praise be to God in every circumstance, and let him say: May God have mercy on you, and let him say: May God forgive me and you. And he continued with Zaydah. Ibn Qudamah, Sufyan Al-Thawri, based on his narration on the authority of Mansour,"
"7697","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr told us, Muawiyah bin Amr told us, Zaydah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of a man, from Al-Nakha’, who said: We were with Salim bin Ubaid on a journey, and he mentioned a hadith as long as a hadith. Al-Thawri “It was narrated by Jarir bin Abdul-Hamid, on the authority of Mansour, based on the illusion, so the unknown man attributed Al-Nakha’i between Hilal bin Yasaf and Salem bin ""slaves"""
"7698","Professor Abu Al-Walid told us, Ibrahim bin Ali told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, he said: Muhammad bin Nu’aym told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim, they said: Jarir reported, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, he said: We were with Salim bin Ubaid, on a journey, when a man from among the people sneezed. He said: Peace be upon you. Salem said: Peace be upon you and your mother. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “If one of you sneezes... Let him praise God and let those who are with him say: May God have mercy on you, and let him respond to them: May God forgive us and you. The illusion in this narration of Jarir is apparent. Hilal bin Yassaf did not catch up with Salim bin Ubaid and did not see him, and there was an unknown man between them. As for the statement that occurred by some jurists who did not He distinguishes between true and false reports regarding the command of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to say to the one who was gloating: May God guide you and put your mind at ease. So it is misled that this gloating is for the People of the Book and not the Muslims.”"
"7699","So Muhammad bin Ali bin Duhaym Al-Shaybani told us, in Kufa, Ahmed bin Hazim bin Abi Gharza told us, Abu Nu’aym, and Qabisah told us, They said: Sufyan told us, Hakim bin Al-Daylam told us, Abu Burdah told us, Abu Musa told us, may God be pleased with him. He said: The Jews used to sneeze at The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, hoped that he would say to them: May God have mercy on you, and he used to say to them: “May God guide you and set your mind right.” This is a related hadith. The chain of transmission, and this news is not contrary to the authentic narrations agreed upon in the two authentic collections of the two Imams Muhammad ibn Ismail and Muslim bin Al-Hajjaj, because one of the correct Sunnahs is for a Muslim to say to his sneezing brother: May God have mercy on you, and he responds by saying: May God guide you and put your mind right. This indicates what the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded to say to a Muslim when he sneezes: May God have mercy on you. The one who uses that as evidence is not Distinguishing between a sneezer and a gloater, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed for guidance for himself and for the Muslims in many long-lasting reports. Explained in this place, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered his friend, his successor, and his circumciser, Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, to “He asks God for guidance.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7699 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7700","As Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, in Marw, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Al-Nadr bin Shumail told us, Shu’bah reported, On the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Ali, ask God for guidance and protection, and remember “With guidance I will guide you on the path and with payment you will direct the arrow.” Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded his son Al-Hasan bin Ali, the master of the youth of the people of Paradise according to what his father, may God be pleased with them, commanded.” The hadith of Yazid bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Abu Al-Jawza, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ali, in The supplication of Qunoot that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught: “O God, guide me among those whom You have guided.” It is too famous for its chain of transmission and its methods to be mentioned. We returned to “Authentic news in morals that were not produced by the two imams.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7700 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7701","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade a man to place one of his legs on The other while he was lying down.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7701 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7702","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abdullah bin Salih told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told me, Abu Al-Zubair narrated to me, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “He forbade the inclusion of the deaf one and raising The man had one leg over the other while lying on his back.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7702 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7703","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Ubaid bin Sharik Al-Bazzar told us, Amr bin Khalid Al-Harrani told us, Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, On the authority of Ibrahim ibn Maysara, on the authority of Amr ibn al-Sharid, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by him while he was leaning on He placed his hand behind his back and said: “The seat of one who is angry at them will sit.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7703 - True"
"7704","Ali bin Hamshadh told me, Ubaid bin Sharik Al-Bazzar told us, Abu Al-Jamahir Muhammad bin Uthman Al-Tanukhi told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad told us, On the authority of Musab bin Thabit, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is good “The councils are the widest.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7704 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7705","Ali ibn Hamshadh told me, Muhammad ibn Shadhan al-Jawhari told me, Mu’alla ibn Mansur al-Razi told me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Mawwal told me, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Amra, that Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, called for a funeral among his people, and he came and the people gathered When they saw him, they came out to him and he sat in a corner and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best gatherings are the broadest ones.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7705 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7706","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Muhammad bin Muawiyah told us, Mazadaf bin Ziyad Al-Madani, he said: And he praised him well, saying: I heard Muhammad bin Ka’b Al-Qurazi saying: I met Omar bin Abdul Aziz, in Medina in His youth, beauty, and youth. He said: When he left behind, I approached him and asked him for permission, and he allowed me to look at him and he said to me: Oh Ibn Ka'b, why do I see you staring so hard? I said: O Commander of the Faithful, when I see the change in your color and the thinness of your body and the discoloration of your hair. He said: O Ibn Ka’b, how about if you see me again? Three are in my grave, and the ants have snatched up my eyeballs and run down my cheeks, and my nostrils and mouth are smeared with pus. You would have been my most severe denial. Let that one speak to me. Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed There is honor for everything, and the most honorable of sitting is that with which one faces the Qiblah, and that you sit among yourselves in honesty, and kill the snake and the scorpion. And if you are in your prayer and do not cover your walls, and none of you looks at his brother’s letter except with his permission, and none of you prays behind ""Sleeping and not speaking""
He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about the best deeds for God Almighty? He said: “Whoever brings joy to a believer has either fed him from his hunger, or paid off a debt for him, or relieved him of the distress of this world, will be relieved of the distress of this world.” May God protect him from the distress of the Hereafter, and whoever spares a well-off or overlooks a hardship, God will shade him on the Day when there will be no shade but His shade, and whoever walks with his brother in towards the village to satisfy his need. God Almighty will establish his foot on the day the feet will move, and for one of you to walk with his brother to make up for His need is better than that he seclude himself in this mosque of mine for two months - and he pointed with his finger - Shall I not inform you of your wickedness? They said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “He who descends alone and prevents his supplication and flogs his servant.” This hadith has another chain of transmission with the addition of letters in it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7706 - Hero of the Hadith"
"7707","I heard Abu Sa`id al-Khalil bin Ahmad al-Qadi, in the house of Prince al-Saydid Abu Salih Mansour bin Nuh, in his presence, shouting the narration of this The hadith, and he said: Abu Al-Qasim Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Baghawi told us, Ubaid Allah bin Muhammad Al-Aishi told us, Abu Al-Miqdam Hisham bin Ziyad, Muhammad bin Ka’b Al-Qurazi told us, he said: I witnessed Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who is our ruler in Medina, following Al-Walid bin Abdul Malik. He was a thick, stocky young man. When he left, I brought him with my little fingers and entered upon him while he had gone through what he had gone through, and lo and behold, he had changed. His condition as it was, then he mentioned the hadith and added to it: “And whoever looks in his brother’s book without his permission, it is as if he were looking into Hell, and whoever loves If he is the strongest of people, let him rely on God, and whoever loves to be the most generous of people, let him fear God Almighty, and whoever loves to be the richest of people Let what is in the hand of God be more reliable than what is in His hand.” And he said: “Shall I inform you of something worse than this?” They said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “Whoever does not say an offense, does not accept an excuse, or forgives a sin, should I inform you of something worse than this?” They said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “Whoever’s goodness is not hoped for and whose evil is not believed. Indeed, Jesus, son of Mary, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, rose up among the Children of Israel and said: O my son. Israel: Do not speak the wisdom of an ignorant person, lest you be unjust to it. Do not withhold its people from it, lest you wrong them. Do not wrong an unjust, and you will not repay Unjust, then your bounty will be nullified before your Lord. O Children of Israel, there are three matters: a matter whose wrongdoing has become clear, so avoid it, and a matter in which there is disagreement, so reject it. To God Almighty, “This is an authentic hadith. Hisham bin Ziyad Al-Nasri and Musadfid bin Ziyad Al-Madini agreed on a narration on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka'b Al-Qurazi, and God knows best, and I did not find it necessary to evacuate this place from him, as he had collected a lot of literature."
"7708","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazid Al-Bayruti told me, my father told me, Al-Awza’i told me, he told me Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Qays al-Ghifari, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us while we were in The row after sunset, and he said: “O so-and-so, go with so-and-so, and oh so-and-so, go with so-and-so,” until I remained five, of whom I was the fifth. So he said: “Get up.” With me.” So we did so, and we went to Aisha, may God be pleased with her, and that was before the veil came down. He said: “O Aisha, feed us.” So she approached. Then he said: “O Aisha, feed us.” She brought a bunch of grass like peat, then he said: “O Aisha, give us something to drink.” So she brought a bunch of grass, then he said: “If you wish, you can sleep with us, and if you wish, you can go to the mosque and sleep in it.” He said: So we slept in the mosque, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me. He greeted me at the end of the night and made me sleep on my stomach, so he pushed me with his foot and said: “What is the matter with you when this sleep is a sleep that God hates?” Or he hates it.” This is a different hadith in its chain of transmission on Yahya bin Abi Katheer, and the end of it is that the correct one is Qays bin Tukhfa al-Ghifari. This is witnessed by the hadith of Abu Hurairah"
"7709","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by a man lying on his stomach and hit him. with his foot and said: “It is a lie that God Almighty does not like.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7709 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7710","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Hisham bin Ali told us, Abdullah bin Raja told us, Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Kathir bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Iyad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade a man from sitting between the sun and the shade.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7710 - True"
"7711","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz told us, in Kufa, Ahmed bin Musa bin Ishaq Al-Tamimi told us, Munjab bin Al-Harith told us, Ali bin Mushar, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw me He greeted me while I was sitting in the sun and said: “Come to the shade, for it is blessed.”"
"7712","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq Al-Basri told us, in Egypt, Abu Dawud told us, and Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw my father while he was sitting in the sun. So he said: “He turned to the shadow, for he is blessed.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and if Shu’bah sent him, then it is Manjab bin Al-Harith and Ali bin Mushar. ""Two trusts"""
"7713","Abd al-Samad bin Ali al-Bazzar told us, in Baghdad, Hamid bin Sahl told us, Amr bin Marzuq told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abd Rabbuh. Ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Abdullah, the client of Abu Musa al-Ash’ari, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Abi al-Hasan, who said: We were in a house in the presence of a witness, and he entered upon us. Abu Bakra, then a man stood up to him from where he was sitting, and Abu Bakra, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A man should not stay The man from his sitting place, then he sits in it, and do not wipe your hand on the garment of someone whom you do not own.” The two sheikhs agreed on the hadith of standing up and did not produce a hadith. “The garment, and it has a valid chain of narration.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7713 - True"
"7714","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us about Marw, Abd Al-Aziz bin Hatim told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Abu Tamila, Abu Al-Munib Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah Al-Atki narrated to me, Abdullah bin Buraidah narrated to me, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, he said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade two sittings and two places of clothing: As for the two sittings between the shade and the sun, and the other sitting is for you to hide in. A garment that exposes your private parts, and the two types of clothing: one is that you pray in a garment and do not wear a scarf with it, and the other is that you pray in trousers when you do not have a garment on. """
"7715","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Uthman bin Omar told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Maysara bin Habib, On the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Aisha bint Talha, on the authority of Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, may God be pleased with her, she said: “I have never seen anyone more like She said: “And whenever she entered upon the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he would rise up to her, kiss her, and make her sit in his seat. He entered upon her, and she rose from her seat, kissed him, and made him sit in her seat.”
When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, fell ill, Fatima entered and bent over him, then raised her head, and wept, then bent over him and raised her head. She laughed and I said: I thought that this was one of the wisest of our women, so she is one of the women. When he died, I said to her: I saw you when you were depressed. At the Prophet, so you raised your head and cried, then you turned to him, so you raised your head and laughed. What made you do that? She said: “When Nadhira told me that he had died from this pain, I cried. Then he told me that I would rush his family to catch up with him.” That is when I laughed.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context. Rather, they agreed on the hadith of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq. On the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her,
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7715 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7716","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad bin Ismail told us about Al-Ray, Abu Hatim told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Muthanna told us. Al-Ansari, my father told me, on the authority of Thumama, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, “Whenever the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, spoke With a word that he repeated three times so that it could be attributed to him. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7716 - It was included by Al-Bukhari, except for his saying, “You should reason with it.”"
"7717","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Shazan Al-Jawhari told us, Mu’alla bin Mansour told us, Hushaym told us, Mansour told us Ibn Zazan, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Al-Ala’ Ibn Al-Hadrami, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, “He wrote to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him So he began to himself, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7717 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7718","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ubayy, and Shuaib bin Al-Layth told us, they said: He informed us Al-Layth, on the authority of Khalid bin Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hilal, on the authority of Utbah bin Muslim, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, that he entered upon Abdul-Malik Ibn Marwan, and he said: Do you count the names of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, which Jubayr ibn Mut’im used to count? He said: “Yes, they are six: Muhammad, Ahmad, Khatam, Hashīr, Aqīb, and Māḥah. As for Hashīr, he will be sent with the Hour {a warner to you before me.” A severe punishment} [Saba: 46], and as for the one who punishes, it is he who follows the prophets, and as for the one who erases, then it is God who erases with him the misdeeds of those who follow him. “This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7718 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7719","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz, Muhammad bin Ghalib, and Ali bin Al-Saqr Al-Sukari told us, they said: Thana Ibrahim bin Ziyad Sablan, Abbad bin Abbad Al-Muhallabi, Ubad Allah bin Omar told us, in Medina, and his brother Abdullah in Mecca in the year One hundred and forty-four, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I love your names.” “To God Almighty, ‘Abdullah and ‘Abd al-Rahman.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7719 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7720","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Al-Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ali bin Saleh Al-Makki, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Indeed, the most beloved of your names to God Almighty are Abdullah and Abdul-Rahman.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7720 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7721","Abdullah bin Saad Al-Hafiz told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, and Muhammad bin Bashar told us, they said: Abu Ahmad, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Omar, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If I live... God willing, they will be forbidden to be called Rabah, Aflah, Najih, and Yasar, and if I live, God willing, I will expel the Jews from the Arabian Peninsula.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it. I do not know of anyone who narrated it on the authority of Al-Thawri who mentions Omar in his chain of transmission other than Abu Ahmad.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7721 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7722","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Humaid bin Ayyash Al-Ramli told us, Ma’mal bin Ismail told us, Sufyan told us, and Abu Al-Abbas Al-Mahboubi told us, Ahmad bin Sayyar told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Sufyan told us, Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad told us Ibn Ghalib, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If I live, he will have forbidden it to be called a blessing, a benefit, and a relief,” so he died without forbidding it. Narrated by Al-Mu’mal ibn Ismail in his hadith, and I do not know. He said: Rafi’ or not?"
"7723","Abu Al-Ziyad bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, Abu Al-Zannad told us, on the authority of Al-Araj, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The most humble of names in the sight of God on the Day of Resurrection is a man called a king.” The possessions of Shahan Shah.” Sufyan said: “When the non-Arabs venerate their king, they say, ‘Shahan Shah: You are the king of kings.’” This is an authentic hadith based on The condition of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it because a group of Sufyan’s companions narrated it on his authority with a chain of transmission on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who reported it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7723 - They brought it out"
"7724","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told us, Musa bin Al-Hasan told us, Hawdha bin Khalifa told us, Awf told us, on the authority of Khalas, and Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Huraira, may God be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The wrath of God became intense against a man whom the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, killed. And the wrath of God intensified against a man who was called the King of Kings. “There is no king but God Almighty.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7724 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7725","Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us about Hamdan, Abu Hatim al-Razi told us, Sa`id bin Marwan al-Zahrani told us, Issam bin Bashir, my father told me, he said: My people, Banu al-Harith ibn Ka’b, sent me to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. When I came to him, he said to me: “Hello, what’s the matter? Your name? I said: Many. He said: “Rather, you are good tidings.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7725 - True"
"7726","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Yahya, who is Ibn Sa’id, told us, on the authority of Zakaria bin Abi Zaida, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muti’ bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he greeted the Day of Conquest, saying: “No Quraysh will be killed after this day out of patience until the Day of Resurrection.” He said: “And none of the disobedient ones will catch up.” Quraysh, Islam other than my father. “He brings him out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7726 - True"
"7727","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Hisham bin Ali Al-Sadusi told us, Muadh bin Hani told us, Abdullah bin Al-Harith bin Abza told us Al-Makki, Rayta bint Muslim told me, on the authority of her father, that he witnessed Hunayn with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “What is your name?” He said: A crow. He said: “Your name is Muslim.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7727 - True"
"7728","Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told me, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told me, and Abu Omar told me Ibn Matar, Al-Adl, Yahya Ibn Muhammad Al-Bakhtari told us, Ubayd Allah Ibn Muadh told us, Ubayy told us, Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq, He narrates on the authority of Khaythamah: “His grandfather named his father ‘Aziz, so he mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he named him Abdul Rahman.” The chain of transmission is authentic and it is not “He brings him out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7728 - True"
"7729","Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, Bashir bin Maymun told us, On the authority of his uncle, Usama bin Akhudri, that a man from Banu Shuqra called: Asram was among the group who came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he came to him. With an Ethiopian boy of his who he bought in that country, and he said: O Messenger of God, I bought this, and I would like you to name him and pray for him. With blessing. He said: “What is your name?” He said: “Asram.” He said: “You are a plant, so what do you want?” He said: This boy's name. He said: “He is Asim,” and he cupped his palm. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7729 - True"
"7730","Abu Bakr bin Quraysh told us, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Abu Al-Rabi’ Al-Zahrani told us, Abu Qutayba Salam bin Qutayba told us, Hamal told us Bin Bashir bin Abi Hadrad, my uncle told me, on the authority of Abu Hadrad, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who drives our camels? “This?” Then a man got up and said: I am. He said: “What is your name?” He said: So-and-so. He said: “Sit down.” Then another got up and said: “I.” He said: “What is your name?” He said: So-and-so. He said: “Sit down.” Then another got up and said: “I.” He said: “What is your name?” He said: Najiya. He said: “You are hers, so give her drink.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7730 - True"
"7731","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Muhammad bin Amr al-Hurashi told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Ibrahim bin Saad told me, he told me My father, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: “In pre-Islamic times my name was Abd Amr, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, named me Abdul Rahman “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7731 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7732","Abu Sa`id Ahmad ibn Ya`qub al-Thaqafi told us, Abu Muslim told us, Amr ibn Marzuq told us, Imran al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurarah bin Awfa, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to a man: “What is your name?” He said: Shihab. He said: “You are Hisham.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. And then the man Hisham bin Amer Al-Ansari """"
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7732 - True"
"7733","Abdul Rahman bin Hamdan Al-Jallab told us, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Al-Mu’alla bin Rashid told us, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Al-Mukhtar told us, He said: Ali bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Hisham bin Amer, may God be pleased with him, who said: I came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: “What is your name?” I said: Shihab. He said: “Rather, you are Hisham.”"
"7734","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman, the jurist in Baghdad, informed us, Hilal bin Al-Alaa Al-Ruqi told us, Ubayy told us, Ubayd Allah bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, that he named his eldest son after his uncle Hamza and he named him Hussein By his uncle Jafar. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called Ali, may God be pleased with him, and said: “I have been ordered to change the name of these two,” and he said: “By God.” And His Messenger knows best, so he named them Hasan and Husayn. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration,” but they did not narrate it."
"7735","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Al-Nadr bin Shumail told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, Mansour, Suleiman, and Husayn bin Abdul Rahman said: We heard Salem bin Abi Al-Jaad, speaking on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with him. About them, he said: A son was born to the Ansar, and they wanted to name him Muhammad, so they brought him to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “You have done well.” “The Ansar, call me by my name and do not conceal my nickname, for I have been sent as a judge to swear among you.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. In it, they agreed on the hadith of Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, in another context, and Bishr ibn Umar al-Zahrani and Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi combined it on the authority of “A division between the four, just as Al-Nadr bin Al-Shumayl brought them together.”"
"7736","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Saadi told us, Bishr bin Omar Al-Zahrani told us, he said: Yahya told us Ibn Muhammad Ibn Yahya, Abu Al-Walid told us, they said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Sulayman, Husayn, Mansur, and Qatada. They heard Salem Ibn Abi Al-Jaad, narrated on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, a similar story.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7735 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7737","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Nasr told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, and Abu Ghassan told us: Fitr bin told us. Caliph, Mundhir Al-Thawri told me, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, saying: I heard my father, saying: I said: O Messenger of God, did you see that a son was born to me? After you, I will have a son whom I will name after your name and give him your nickname. He said: “Yes.” Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: “So this was a concession for me.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it. Perhaps He is delusional and imagines that the two sheikhs did not narrate it from Fitr, and this is not the case, for they have linked it with another in a single chain of narration. Some of our imams have mentioned in this regard a major chapter regarding the permissibility of calling upon one’s wife by her name, contrary to the common opinion that it is not permissible. He mentioned many reports in it regarding the saying of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: O Aisha, O Aisha, O Umm Salamah, and her estate, because they agreed on “Most of them”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7737 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7738","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Sabiq Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Yahya bin Abdullah told us Bin Salem, and Saeed bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Abbad bin Hamza, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that she She said: O Messenger of God, won’t you give me a nickname? He said: “Give me the nickname of your son, Abdullah bin Al-Zubair,” and her nickname was Umm Abdullah. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7738 - True"
"7739","Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us about Hamdan, Hilal bin al-Alaa al-Ruqi told us, Ubayy told us, Ubayd Allah bin Amr told us, about Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Hamza bin Suhaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, that he said to Suhaib: You are a man if it were not for three qualities. He said: What are they? He said: You have become a child but you have no children. You belong to the Arabs and you are a Roman man, and you are extravagant in food. He said: O Commander of the Faithful, as for your saying: You have become a daughter-in-law and have no children, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called Kanani Abu Yahya. Your statement: You belonged to the Arabs and you are a man from the Byzantines. I am a man from Nimr bin Qasit. I stayed in Mosul after I was a boy. My family and lineage, and as for your saying: There is extravagance in food, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Indeed, the best of you is he who feeds himself with food.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7739 - True"
"7740","Makram bin Ahmad al-Qadi told us, in Baghdad, Yahya bin Ja’far bin al-Zabarqan told us, Abd al-Wahhab bin Ata told us, Abu Al-Minhal Abd al-Rahman bin Muawiyah al-Bakrawi, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Abi Bakra, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, he said: When he was besieged The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, at Taif, I hung a pulley, and he said: “How did you do?” I said: I hung with a pulley. He said: “You are Abu Bakra.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7740 - True"
"7741","Muhammad bin Ali Al-Shaybani told me, in Kufa, Ahmad bin Hazim Al-Ghafari told us, Abu Ghassan told us, Qays bin Al-Rabi’ told us, on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Shurayh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “Which of your sons is the eldest?” I said: Shurayh. He said: “So you are Abu Shurayh.” Qais was the only one who narrated it, on the authority of Al-Miqdam, and I remember after him a hadith that was unique to Mujalid bin Sa’id and not them. From the condition of this book """"
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7741 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7742","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Stolen. He said: I came to Omar, and he said: What is your name? I said: stolen. He said: whose son? I said: Ibn Al-Ajda’. He said: You are Masruq bin Abdul Rahman. “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told us that Al-Ajda’ is a devil.” He said: “His name in the court was Masruq bin Abdul Rahman.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7742 - Qais and Mujalid are not among the conditions of our book"
"7743","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Ahmad bin Yahya told us, Adi bin Al-Fadl told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Suwayd, on the authority of Yahya bin Yamar, On the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: A man said: O Messenger of God. He said: “O Labayk!” This is an authentic hadith, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7743 - Adi bin Al-Fadl left him"
"7744","Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Sahl Al-Faqih told us in Bukhara, Saleh bin Muhammad Al-Hafiz told us, Shayban told us, Sulayman bin Al-Mughirah told us, Thabit Al-Bunani, on the authority of Shuaib bin Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them, said: “The Messenger of God God, may God bless him and grant him peace, hates for anyone to step on his heel, but on the right and the left.”"
"7745","Abu Nasr told us, Ali bin Al-Hussein Al-Darhami told us, Umayyah bin Khalid told us, Sulayman bin Al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a similar hadith Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah “is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7745 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7746","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Bahr bin Bari told us, my father told me, Saeed bin Maslamah bin Hisham bin Abdul Malik Umayyad, Ismail bin Umayyah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with him About them, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the mosque with Abu Bakr on his right and Omar on his left, taking them by the hand, and he said: “This is how we will be raised on the Day of Resurrection.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7746 - Saeed bin Maslama, they weak him"
"7747","Yahya bin Mansour Al-Qadi told us, Abu Amr Ahmad bin Al-Mubarak Al-Mustamli told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Salam informed us Ibn Qutayba, Dawud Ibn Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade The man walked between the two women.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not make him go out."
"7748","Muhammad bin Thabit Al-Bunani, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Anas, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade a man to walk between two camels, leading them.” Sahih. “Attribution”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7748 - Muhammad bin Thabit’s weakness"
"7749","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Attab Al-Abdi told us, Abu Qalaba Abdul-Malik bin Muhammad told us, Saeed bin Amir told us, Shubail bin Ezra, he said: We set off with his money to Anas, and we were young, so we entered upon him and he said: How good this is, then he spoke. With words that would encourage them to seek knowledge, he said: He told us on that day that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The example of a righteous companion is that of a perfumer.” If he does not give you some of his perfume - or he said: If you do not get some of his perfume - then he will give you some of his scent. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7749 - True"
"7750","Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Nusayr al-Khalidi told us, Yahya bin Ayyub al-Alaf told us, in Egypt, Sa`id bin Abi Maryam told us, Yahya bin Ayoub, Humaid al-Tawil told me, he said: I heard Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, saying: “Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, walked As if he was leaning.” Ibn Abi Maryam said: Yahya bin Ayyub told us, Humaid al-Taweel told me, he said: I heard Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he says: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, walked, it was as if he were leaning.” Ibn Abi Maryam said: And someone else than Ibn Ayyub informed us. With the hadith, he said: “As if he is being sufficient.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7750 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7751","Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrifi told us, about Marw, Abu Qalaba told us, Quraysh bin Anas told us, Ash’ath told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “He forbade walking between two fingers.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7751 - True"
"7752","Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us, Muhammad bin Ali bin Affan told us, Qubaisa bin Uqba told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qais, on the authority of Nabih Al-Anazi, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He left his house, and we walked before him and left him behind him to the angels.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7752 - Al-Dhahabi said it is authentic"
"7753","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, Shu’bah told us, On the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qais, on the authority of Nabih Al-Anzi, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do not walk in front of me or behind me, for this is the place of the angels.” Jabir said: “I came running to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, as if I were a spark.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7753 - True"
"7754","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Dhuhli told us, Musaddad told us, Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Majliz, said: Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, saw a person sitting in the middle of a group and said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed “Whoever sits in the middle of a group” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7754 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7755","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Ismail bin Ulayya told us, on the authority of Dawud Ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, Abu Jubayrah Ibn Al-Dahhak narrated to us, saying: About us, it was revealed about Banu Salamah: “And do not call one another by nicknames” [Al-Hujurat: 11]. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and there was not a man among us who did not have two or three names.” He said: “Then the man was called and they said, ‘Mah, Mim, Mim. He becomes angry because of this.” So it was revealed: “And do not call one another by nicknames” [Al-Hujurat: 11] “The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7755 - True"
"7756","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakkar bin Qutaybah Al-Qadi told us, Safwan bin Issa told us, Unays bin Abi Yahya told us, about His father, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came out to us during his illness in which he died while he was bound. The head, he said: So I followed him until he ascended the pulpit, he said: Then he said: “At this time I will be standing at the basin.” Then he said: “Indeed, a servant has been offered the world.” And her adornment, so he chose the Hereafter.” And no one among the people thought of that except Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, and he said: May my mother and father be sacrificed for you. We will sacrifice ourselves, our children, our wealth, and our loyalists to you. He said: Then he descended from the pulpit, and he was not seen until now. “This is an authentic hadith on the authority of The condition of the two Sheikhs and the purpose in presenting it in this book is to make it permissible for people to say to one another, “My soul and my ransom is mine for you, or may I be made your ransom” Or your ransom and anything similar. And watch this hadith.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7756 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7757","What Abu Al-Abbas Al-Sayyari told us, Muhammad bin Musa bin Hatim Al-Bashani told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Al-Hussein bin Waqid told us, Abdullah bin Buraidah told me, he said: I heard Abu Buraidah saying: I was in the mosque and Abu Musa al-Ash’ari was reciting, then the Messenger of God came out May God’s prayers and peace be upon him and said: “Who is this?” So I said: I, Buraida, have made ransom for you, O Prophet of God. He said: “This was given from the Psalms of the family of David.” This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs did not narrate it in this context and from that.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7757 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7758","What Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Yunus Al-Dhabi told us, Muhammad bin Ubaid Al-Tanafisi told us, Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, on the authority of Hilal bin Khabbab, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them, he said: We were around the Messenger of God, may God bless him. He said the salutation sitting down when he mentioned the sedition or it was mentioned to him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you see the people, their covenants have been canceled. And their trustworthiness diminished, and they were like this.” He clasped his fingers together, so I stood up to him and said: How should I do, O Messenger of God, may God make me your ransom? He said: “Stay at home, control your tongue, take what you know and leave what you disapprove of, and you must deal exclusively with the affairs of yourself and leave behind the affairs of the people.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7758 - True"
"7759","Abu Amr bin Al-Sammak told us, Yahya bin Ja’far told us, Ali bin Asim told us, Khaled Al-Hadha’ told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Al-Araj, On the authority of Abdullah bin Mughaffal, may God be pleased with him, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the killing.” He said: Then a man with him was kidnapped and he said: “I will tell you on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and you will ignore it. By God, I will never speak to you.” The two sheikhs agreed to narrate the hadith of Uqba ibn Sahban, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mughaffal, regarding the prohibition of cutting, but they did not narrate it in this context, and it is an authentic chain of narration, and something like it has been narrated. On the authority of Ibn Umar"
"7760","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Khalid bin Abdul Rahman told us, Habib bin Sulaym told us, on the authority of Amr bin Muslim, he said: A man was kidnapped by Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, and he said: Do not commit fraud, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbidding About deception.” Then Ibn Umar saw him deceit after that and said: “I informed you that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbids deception.” Then I swear I will never speak to you again."
"7761","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ali bin Bakr Al-Sahmi told us, Abu Yunus Hatim bin Abi Saghira told us, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, on the authority of Abu Saleh, The servant of Umm Hani, on the authority of Umm Hani, may God be pleased with her, that she asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, she said: I said: O Messenger of God, Have you seen the words of God, Blessed and Most High: {And you commit evil in your midst} [Al-Ankabut: 29]. What was that evil that they used to commit? He said: “They used to mock the people of the way and kidnap them.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7761 - True"
"7762","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us, Muhammad bin Maslamah Al-Wasiti told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yasar, on the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “When you hear the barking of dogs and the braying of donkeys at night, seek refuge in God from the accursed Satan, for she sees what you do not see.” And go out as little as possible when it happens, for God Almighty spreads from His creation whatever He wills during His night, and close the doors and mention the name of God over them. Satan does not open a false door and the name of God is mentioned over it, and lean the waterers and cover the jars and cover the vessels.” This is an authentic hadith. On the condition of a Muslim, and they did not take it out in this context.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7762 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7763","Abu Aoun Muhammad bin Ahmad al-Jazzar told me, Ali al-Saffar told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Hajjaj told us, Hammad told us, about Habib, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Lock up your children when Foua’ah goes away.” “Isha’, for it is an hour in which the devils penetrate.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7763 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7764","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Qantari told me, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Hakim, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Beware of sleeping in the dark after the end of the night.” For you do not know what God brings from His creation.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7764 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7765","Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Khuza’i told us about Mecca, which God Almighty protected. Abu Yahya bin Abi Masarra told us, Nafi’ bin Yazid, Ibn al-Haad told me, that Nafi’ told him on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, may God be pleased with them both, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: “Do not let fire linger in your houses, for it is an enemy.” Ibn Umar would not lie down until he did not let a fire into the house unless he extinguished it. The last member of the house to sleep was praying, and when he finished he would not sleep until he extinguished the lamp. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7765 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7766","Abu Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saffar told us, Al-Adl told us, Ahmad bin Nasr told us, Amr bin Talha Al-Qannad told us, Asbat bin Nasr, on the authority of Simak ibn Harb, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: A mouse came and started pulling the wick. So the maid went to rebuke her, and the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Leave her.” So she brought her and threw her in the hands of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. peace be upon him, which he was sitting on, and from it burned the place of a dirham, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When you sleep, extinguish “Your lamps, for Satan brings something like this to this and will burn you.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7766 - True"
"7767","Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Khorasani, Al-Adl, told us, Ahmad bin Ziyad bin Mihran told us, Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, Sulayman bin Sufyan Al-Madini, Bilal bin Yahya bin Talha bin Ubaid Allah narrated to me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him When he saw the crescent, he said: “O God, make it crescent upon us with security, faith, safety, and Islam, my Lord and your Lord.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7767 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7768","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Hibban bin Hilal told us, Ja’far bin Sulayman told us, Thabit told us, On the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, that when the sky rained, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would lower his garment from his back until It was raining, and it was said to him: Why are you doing this? He said: “It is a hadith about a covenant with his Lord, the Mighty and Majestic.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7768 - This is in Muslim"
"7769","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Sharik bin Bakr told us, Al-Awza’i told me, Ibn Shihab told me, Thabit Al-Zarqi said that Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, said: A wind blew people away on the road to Mecca, and Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, was a Hajj. It became intense for them, and Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, said to those around him: What is the smell? They did not return anything to him, so I was informed of what Omar had asked about, so I urged my mount until I caught up with him and said: O Commander of the Faithful, I was informed that you You asked about the wind, and I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The wind is from the Spirit of God Almighty. It brings mercy and brings punishment, so no “You should revile it, ask God for its goodness, and seek refuge in God from its evil.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7769 - True"
"7770","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl told us, Jeddi told us, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, Al-Mughirah bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Yazid. Ibn Abi Ubaid, on the authority of Salamah Ibn Al-Akwa’, he narrated it as a chain of transmission, God willing, that when the wind was strong, he would say: “O God, make this one fertile, not sterile.” An authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7770 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7771","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan Al-Harbi told us, Affan told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abd Al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to often mention Khadija, may God be pleased with her. I said: God has succeeded you - and Hammad may have said: God has succeeded you - one of the old women of Quraysh, with red cheeks. She perished in the first era. He said: “Then his face became red with a expression that I had never seen except when the revelation came down and when he saw the appearance of thunder and lightning. Until he knows whether it is mercy or punishment.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7771 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7772","Abu Bakr bin Balwayh told me, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan told us, Affan told us, Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, Abu Matar told us, on the authority of Salem, On the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard thunder and lightning, he would say: “Oh God, do not kill us.” “With Your wrath, and do not destroy us with Your torment, and protect us before that.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7772 - True"
"7773","Muhammad ibn Ali al-San’ani informed us, in Mecca, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Muammar informed us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: We had dinner with Abu Qatada, at the back of a house of ours, and a star descended and we followed our sight, but he forbade us, and said: “Do not follow Your eyes, for we used to forbid that.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7773 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7774","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Abu Hani told me, on the authority of Amr bin Malik al-Janabi, on the authority of Fadalah bin Ubaid, on the authority of Ubadah bin al-Samit, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out during a One day he was on his mount and his companions were with him in front of him, and Muadh bin Jabal said: O Prophet of God, will you permit me to come to you on good terms? Breath? He said: “Yes.” So Mu’adh approached him and they all walked away. Mu’adh said: “May my father’s prayers be upon you, O Messenger of God, if he makes our day before yours. Have you seen if Nothing happened and we will not see anything, God willing, so what deeds will we do after you? Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was silent and said: “Jihad for the sake of God.” Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “What an excellent thing is jihad. And the one who has more power over people than that is fasting and charity.” He said: “The best thing is fasting and charity.” So Muadh mentioned every good thing that the son of Adam does. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He brought people back better than that.” He said: What about my father and mother? He brought people better than that. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pointed to him and said: “Silence except for good.” He said: Will we be held accountable for what our tongues have spoken? He said: So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, struck Mu’adh’s thigh, then said: “O Mu’adh, may your mother be bereaved of you - or whatever God wished for someone to say to him.” That - and will people be thrown on their noses into Hell except what their tongues have uttered? So whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him say Good or to remain silent about evil. Speak good and take advantage, and remain silent about evil and be safe. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. The purpose In quoting it in this situation, it is permissible for the learner to pray to his scholar, who quotes from him, that God make his wish before his scholar, for I Before this, I presented authentic reports that make it permissible for people to say: “May God make me your ransom.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7774 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7775","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Suleiman bin Daoud Al-Hashimi told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Abi al-Zanad told us, On the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He forbids anyone to engage in “The man, the man in one garment, and the woman, the woman in one garment.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7775 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7776","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hadrami told us, Ahmad bin Yunus told us, Abu Shihab told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade a woman to have intercourse with a man and a woman.” The man in one garment.” Ibn Abi Laila said: “And I see in him the rebuke and Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila for the sake of the House of Companions From the Ansar and a mufti and jurist in Kufa, when he saw in him a reprimand, he is an example.”"
"7777","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “A man should not be intimate with a man or a woman.” “The Woman” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari. They have agreed unanimously on the authenticity of this hadith.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7777 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"7778","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Omar Al-Hafiz Ibn Al-Jaabi Al-Qadi told us, Abu Shuaib Abdullah bin Al-Hassan told us, Abdul Aziz Bin Yahya, Muhammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, Radi God said about them: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Beware of a house called the pigeon.” They said: O Messenger of God, it removes tuberculosis and is beneficial. The sick person said: “Whoever enters it should cover it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7778 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7779","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Qabbani, and Ibrahim bin Abi told us. Students, they said: Ishaq bin Ibrahim narrated to us, Muadh bin Hisham narrated, my father narrated to me, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, Radi On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever believes in God and the Last Day should not let his unmarried woman enter the bathroom. He who believes in God and the Last Day should not enter the bathroom except with an apron, and whoever believes in God and the Last Day should not sit at a table. “Khamr is administered to her.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7779 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7780","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ali Al-San’ani informed us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abd Al-Razzaq informed us, Sufyan Al-Thawri informed us, about Mansour, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, he said: Women from the people of the Levant entered upon Aisha, may God be pleased with her, and she said: Perhaps you are from the region whose women enter the bath. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Any woman who puts her clothes in other than her husband’s house, for she has torn the veil between her and God Almighty.” It was narrated by Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7780 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7781","Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of Abi Al-Malih, said: Women from the people of the Levant entered upon Aisha, may God be pleased with her, and she said: You are the ones who Entering the bathrooms. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no woman who puts her clothes on other than in her home without tearing the veil between herself and God Almighty” It was narrated on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, like this on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"7782","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told me, he told me Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Darraj Abi Al-Samh, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib, that women entered the house of Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she asked them who You stink? They said: From the people of Homs. She said: From the owners of the bathhouses? They said: Is there harm in it? She said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Any woman who removes her clothes in someone other than her home, God will tear off her curtain.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7782 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7783","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us, Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Abu Salih told us, Al-Layth told me, on the authority of Yaqoub Bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Jubayr, on the authority of Muhammad bin Thabit bin Shurahbil al-Qurashi, from Banu Abd al-Dar, that Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Khattami told him on the authority of Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever believes In God and the Last Day, let him honor his guest, and whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him honor his neighbor, and whoever believes in God And on the Last Day, let him not enter the baths except with an apron, and whoever of your wives believes in God and the Last Day, let him not enter the baths.” So he was raised. The hadith to Omar bin Abdul Aziz, so he wrote to Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm to ask Muhammad bin Thabit about this. Hadith and write what he said. So he did so, and Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote that women should be prevented from bathing. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.” And Ya’qub bin Ibrahim, The one from whom Al-Layth bin Saad narrated is Abu Yusuf Yaqoub bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Jubayr, on the authority of Muhammad bin Thabit Ibn Sharhabeel Al-Qurashi, he mentioned the hadith
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7783 - True"
"7784","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told us, my grandfather told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Nafi’ bin Yazid told us, he told me Yahya bin Abi Usayd, on the authority of Ubaid bin Abi Suwayya, that he heard Subayah al-Aslamiyah say: Women from the Levant entered upon Aisha. Aisha said: Who are you from? They said: From the people of Homs. She said: The owners of the bathrooms. They said: Yes. Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The dove is forbidden for the women of my nation.”
One of them said: I have daughters whom I can comb with this drink. She said: “With what drink?” She said: Wine. Then Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: “Were you of a good soul to be combed with pig’s blood?” She said: No. She said: “It is like him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7784 - True"
"7785","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq told us, and Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, they said: Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Hammad told us Ibn Salamah, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade handling a drawn sword.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7785 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7786","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Al-Khasib bin Nasih told us, Al-Mubarak bin Fadalah told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by a people who were wielding a drawn sword, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: “May God curse whoever did this. Have I not forbidden this if one of you draws a sword and looks at it and wants to fight it with his brother? Let him sheathe it and then hand it to him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7786 - True"
"7787","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali bin Ahmad bin Alam Al-Saffar told us, in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Wahb bin Jarir, my father told us, he said: I heard Mansour bin Zazan, narrating on the authority of Maymun bin Abi Shabib, on the authority of Qais bin Saad bin Ubadah, that his father He gave him to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to serve him. He said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me while I had prayed two rak’ahs, and he hit me with his foot and said: “Shall I not direct you to one of the gates of Paradise?” I said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “There is no power nor strength except with God.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. The intention in mentioning it in this place was that it is permissible for the father to serve his son, and then it is permissible for the one to whom the service was gifted to employ From him, then it is known about the virtue of Qais bin Saad, may God be pleased with him, that he served the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, until he became of him in the position of the companion of the police, then “He did not leave the Commander of the Faithful, Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, in good times and bad, until he was martyred in front of him on the day of Siffin.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7787 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7788","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Ali al-Shaybani told us about Kufa, Ahmad ibn Hazim al-Ghafari told us, Abu Nu`aym and Abu Ghassan told us, saying: Sharik told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Isa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jubayr, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, who said: He was a Jewish boy. He was serving the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the boy fell ill, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to visit him and said: “O boy, embrace Islam, say there is no god but God.” So the boy started looking at his father, and his father said to him: Say what Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, says to you. He said: There is no god but God, and he accepted Islam and died. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to his companions: “Pray for him.” And the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed for him.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7788 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7789","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Muhammad bin Issa bin Al-Tabbaa told us, Bakkar bin Abd told us Al-Aziz bin Abi Bakra said: I heard my father narrating on the authority of Abi Bakra, may God be pleased with him: That the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought good tidings to him. He gave him good news of the triumph of his horses while his head was in Aisha’s lap, may God be pleased with her. So he stood up and bowed down to God Almighty, prostrating. When he left, he began to ask. The Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Men were destroyed when they obeyed me.” Women” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. And his evidence is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7789 - True"
"7790","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, on the authority of Humaid, On the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, may God be pleased with him, he said: God protected me from something I heard from the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when he was informed that the king of Yazan died, so they put a woman in charge of them, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A people ruled by a woman will never prosper.” This is an authentic hadith based on The condition of the two sheikhs and they did not include it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7790 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7791","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Omar bin Hafs bin Ghayath told us, my father told me, Ma’bad bin Khalid told us. Al-Ansari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, who said: Jarir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, entered upon the Messenger of God He, may God bless him and grant him peace, was with his companions, and each man took his seat, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took his cloak and threw it to him. So he received it with his throat and face, kissed it and placed it on his eyes and said: May God honor you as you have honored me, then he placed it on the back of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, then when a noble man comes to him, So let him honor him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it in this context.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7791 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7792","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Yazid bin Zurayi told us, Khaled Al-Hadha told us, on the authority of Abu Tamimah, on the authority of Rudayf The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said that his animal stumbled upon him and he said: “Unfortunate is Satan.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not say miserable.” Satan, for if you say: “Wretched,” Satan grows arrogant and says: “By my power I have struck him down,” and when it is said: “In the name of God,” he despises himself until he becomes like a fly.” A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it, and the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, whom he did not name, is Yazid bin Zuray’, on the authority of Khalid, whom someone else named: Osama Ibn Malik, father of Abu Al-Malih ibn Usama.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7792 - True"
"7793","Ali bin Issa told us, Ahmad bin Najda al-Qurashi told us, Saeed bin Mansour told us, Muhammad bin Hamran told us, Khaled al-Hadha told us, on the authority of Abi Tamimah, on the authority of Abi Al-Malih bin Usama, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: I was the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and our camel stumbled. So I said: Misfortune is Satan. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “Do not say: Misfortune is Satan, for it will grow until it becomes like a house and becomes strong. But say in the name of God, and when you say: In the name of God, he becomes so small that he becomes like flies.”"
"7794","Professor Abu Al-Walid, Abu Amr Al-Hairi, and Abu Bakr bin Quraysh told us, they said: Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Amr bin Sufyan told us. Hafs Al-Shaybani, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Abdul-Jabbar bin Omar Al-Ayli told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, walked, he did not turn around.” Al-Hakim said: “I do not know of anyone who narrated it on the authority of Muhammad b. “The one who is in distress is not Abdul-Jabbar.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7794 - Abdul-Jabbar bin Omar is damaged"
"7795","Ahmad bin Sahl Al-Bukhari told us, Saleh bin Muhammad bin Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Ghaylan told us, Abu Dawud told us, Al-Hakam bin Attiyah, on the authority of Thabit al-Bunani, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “You name your children. “Muhammad, then you curse them.” Al-Hakam Ibn Atiyya alone, on the authority of Thabit.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7795 - Al-Hakam bin Attiyah, some of them trustworthy him, and he is gentle"
"7796","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, “When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would cover his face.” With his hand or his garment, and he lowered his voice into it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7796 - True"
"7797","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Mas’ar told us, on the authority of Thabit bin Ubaid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Khawat ibn Jubayr, he said: “Sleeping at the beginning of the day is rags, the middle of it is good-natured, and the end of it is foolishness.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7797 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7798","Muhammad bin Musa al-Faqih told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin al-Muthanna, and Muhammad bin Bashar told us, they said: Abd told us Al-Rahman, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid Al-Araj, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rawaha, may God be pleased with him He was on a journey, and he came and hurried to his family at night, and behold, something was sleeping with his wife. He took the sword, and his wife said, “This is so-and-so.” She combed me, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came and that was mentioned to him. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do not touch women at night.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7798 - The Mursal"
"7799","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, and Abu Al-Hasan Al-Anazi told us, they said: Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Yazid bin Khalid Al-Ramli told us, Abdullah told us Ibn Wahb, Amr Ibn Al-Harith informed me, on the authority of Darraj Abu Al-Samh, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no forbearing person except one who is prone to stumble, and no one is wise except one who has experience.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration and it is not It is published by “the last book of literature.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7799 - True"
